  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Yemen Joint Response is a 3-year project funded by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs through the Dutch Relief Alliance. It focuses on short-term and longer-term needs in Lahj and Marib. It encompasses multiple sectors, including emergency food security and livelihoods, protection and WASH. It supports vulnerable people in restoring and improving their livelihoods and creating income opportunities to build their resilience in order to cope with the impacts of the ongoing crises as both locations are faced with complex and multi-dimensional humanitarian challenges, including displacement and high levels of food insecurity. Priorities include thedistribution of cash grants for businesses, establishing community-based protection networks, rehabilitation of water supply systems and hygiene promotion activities. As part of this project, Oxfam in Yemen is partnering with two Yemeni organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-41158230" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Care Nederland</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
  </participating-org>
